{"case_desc":"Dr. David Jadwin sued Kern County over his removal as KMC Pathology Department chair, pay cut, paid administrative leave and contract non-renewal; the construction dispute was whether the general "for cause" termination clause of his Core Physician employment agreement, or the incorporated medical staff bylaw permitting removal of a department chair with or without cause, governed his removal from the chairmanship.","clauses":[{"clause_name":"Article IV, Section 1 — Termination of Agreement (para. A)","taxonomy":"1.3","contract_id":"610FSupp2d1129_agreement_for_professional_services","start_line":197,"end_line":199,"text":"1. TERMINATION OF AGREEMENT

A. Core Physician may terminate this Agreement, without cause, upon ninety (90) days' prior written notice to County.","repairs":"Removed markdown heading marks and bold asterisks around the section heading and paragraph A; no wording changed.","opinion_comment_start_line":428,"opinion_comment_end_line":435},{"clause_name":"Article V, Section 11 — Enforcement of Remedies","taxonomy":"1.3","contract_id":"610FSupp2d1129_agreement_for_professional_services","start_line":249,"end_line":251,"text":"11. ENFORCEMENT OF REMEDIES

No right or remedy herein conferred on or reserved to County is exclusive of any other right or remedy herein or by law or equity provided or permitted, but each shall be cumulative of every other right or remedy given hereunder or now or hereafter existing by law or in equity or by statute or otherwise, and may be enforced concurrently or from time to time.","repairs":"Removed markdown heading marks and bold asterisks from the section heading; no wording changed.","opinion_comment_start_line":436,"opinion_comment_end_line":438}]}
